# Peculium — manual API tests (REST Client for VS Code, extension: humao.rest-client)
#
# Run against the ISOLATED test stack only (separate DB peculium_test, port 8081,
# Yahoo finance disabled). NEVER against the dev/prod stack (port 8080, real data).
#
# Start the stack:
#   docker compose -p peculium-test -f docker-compose.test.yml up -d --build python-service backend
#   until curl -s -o /dev/null http://localhost:8081/api/v1/health/prices; do sleep 1; done
#
# Optional — seed prices so the portfolio allocation weights below are non-zero
# (Yahoo is disabled on the test stack, so there is no HTTP writer for prices):
#   docker compose -p peculium-test -f docker-compose.test.yml exec -T postgres psql -U peculium -d peculium_test < tests/seed-prices.sql
#
# Then send each request in order. Stop afterwards:
#   docker compose -p peculium-test -f docker-compose.test.yml down -v
#
# The python-service microservice is intentionally not exposed on the host:
# exercise it through the backend endpoint (auto-resolve + fetch below).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081/api/v1

### 1. Register a user (only needed once, ignore 409 if already exists)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manual@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "name": "Manual Test"
}

### 2. Login and capture the JWT
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manual@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 3. Create an ETF asset WITHOUT ISIN (auto-resolve will fill it in)
# @name createAsset
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ticker": "SMEA.MI",
  "name": "iShares Core MSCI Europe UCITS ETF EUR (Acc)",
  "type": "etf",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

# On a fresh stack this creates the asset (201, body has id).
# If the ticker already exists it returns 409 — the body carries the same id in
# both "id" and "asset_id", so {{assetId}} resolves on reruns too.
@assetId = {{createAsset.response.body.id}}

### 4. Duplicate create — expected: 409 Conflict with {"error": "...already exists...", "id": "<existing id>", "asset_id": "<existing id>"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ticker": "SMEA.MI",
  "name": "iShares Core MSCI Europe UCITS ETF EUR (Acc)",
  "type": "etf",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 5. NEW — fetch ETF exposure (READ-ONLY PREVIEW). The `.MI` suffix is
### stripped and the ISIN is resolved from the ticker (expected IE00B4K48X80) —
### the ISIN is the ONLY thing persisted. countries/regions and GICS sectors
### from JustETF are returned as a preview and NOT stored: same for
### POST /assets/{id}/fetch-exposure (Yahoo sectors) and
### POST /assets/{id}/fetch-morningstar-exposure. Persist them with the "Save"
### buttons / PUT /assets/{id}/exposure.
### NOTE: the raw provider payload is cached in Redis
### (pc:lookup:exposure:justetf:<ISIN>, TTL PECULIUM_EXPOSURE_CACHE_TTL = 7d), so
### reruns answer without calling the provider; append ?refresh=1 to force a
### fresh fetch and rewrite the cache (see 11b3).
# @name fetchEtfExposure
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{assetId}}/fetch-etf-exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Confirm the asset now carries the resolved ISIN
# @name getAsset
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Read the persisted exposure: the fetch above is a preview, so dimensions
### only appear here after an explicit PUT (see 11d). The GET always answers
### with the full canonical lists (zero-filled when nothing was saved).
# @name getExposure
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{assetId}}/exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Create a second ETF asset WITHOUT ISIN (US S&P 500 tracker, EUR share class)
# @name createAsset2
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ticker": "SXR8.DE",
  "name": "iShares Core S&P 500 UCITS ETF EUR (Acc)",
  "type": "etf",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

# On a fresh stack this creates the asset (201, body has id).
# If the ticker already exists it returns 409 — the body carries the same id in
# both "id" and "asset_id", so {{asset2Id}} resolves on reruns too.
@asset2Id = {{createAsset2.response.body.id}}

### 9. Duplicate create — expected: 409 Conflict with {"error": "...already exists...", "id": "<existing id>", "asset_id": "<existing id>"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ticker": "SXR8.DE",
  "name": "iShares Core S&P 500 UCITS ETF EUR (Acc)",
  "type": "etf",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 10. NEW — fetch ETF exposure for the S&P 500 fund (ISIN IE00B5BMR087):
### read-only PREVIEW (regions tilt to North America, sectors to Information
### Technology). Nothing is persisted by the fetch — use PUT /assets/{id}/exposure.
# @name fetchEtfExposure2
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/fetch-etf-exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Read the persisted exposure for SXR8.DE (unchanged by the preview fetch #10)
# @name getExposure2
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11b. NEW — fetch ETF exposure from Morningstar (countries + sectors + official
### regions), also a read-only PREVIEW: nothing is persisted except the resolved
### ISIN; save the preview with PUT /assets/{id}/exposure. Uses the custom
### resolver (headless Chromium bootstrap) in the python-service; falls back to
### 502 if Morningstar is unreachable in the sandbox (Yahoo disabled, external
### calls may be blocked). The raw payload is cached per ISIN under
### pc:lookup:exposure:morningstar:<ISIN> (its own entry, separate from the
### JustETF one), so a rerun is served from Redis and never boots Chromium; use
### 11b3 to force a refetch.
# @name fetchMorningstarExposure
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/fetch-morningstar-exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11b3. Force a provider refetch bypassing the exposure cache: ?refresh=1
### (refresh=true also accepted) skips the Redis read and rewrites the cached
### payload. Works on both prefill endpoints (also /fetch-etf-exposure). The
### cache TTL is PECULIUM_EXPOSURE_CACHE_TTL (default 7 days).
# @name fetchMorningstarRefresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/fetch-morningstar-exposure?refresh=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11b2. NEW — derive regions from countries without persisting (tassonomia
### Morningstar: GB→United Kingdom, JP→Japan, TW/KR→Asia Developed, residuo→Other).
# @name deriveRegions
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/exposure/derive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "countries": [
    { "name": "US", "weight": 40 },
    { "name": "GB", "weight": 25 },
    { "name": "JP", "weight": 12 },
    { "name": "TW", "weight": 10 },
    { "name": "KR", "weight": 5 }
  ]
}

### 11c. Read the persisted exposure: fetches #10/#11b are previews and store
### nothing, so this only reflects what a previous PUT saved (the GET is always
### canonical: zero-filled `countries` across all ~89 canonical ISO codes when
### nothing was stored). Use 11d to persist a preview's values.
# @name getExposure3
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11d. Manual edit of country weights: a small subset (must not exceed ~100; a
### sum below 100 is valid). Saving countries does NOT touch the regions
### dimension: stored regions come back unchanged (recompute them explicitly
### with "Calcola da paesi" / POST /assets/{id}/exposure/derive).
### countries_source records WHERE the saved dimension came from ("morningstar",
### "justetf", "yahoo", ...); optional countries_source / regions_source /
### sectors_source — absent or empty ⇒ "manual". The response (and the GET)
### carries a `provenance` map with source + updated_at per saved dimension.
# @name putCountries
PUT {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "countries": [
    { "name": "US", "weight": 70.0 },
    { "name": "DE", "weight": 15.0 },
    { "name": "FR", "weight": 15.0 }
  ],
  "countries_source": "morningstar"
}

### 11d2. Read back the persisted provenance: the GET now includes
### "provenance": { "countries": { "source": "morningstar", "updated_at": ... } }
### (only for dimensions saved at least once, omitted when empty; fetch previews
### never write it).
# @name getExposureWithProvenance
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{asset2Id}}/exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Create a portfolio (EUR) — id is captured so the allocation and transaction
### requests below need no manual UUID editing, on a fresh stack or on reruns.
# @name createPortfolio
POST {{baseUrl}}/portfolios
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "BitPie portfolio",
  "description": "Manual test portfolio: one European and one US ETF",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

@portfolioId = {{createPortfolio.response.body.id}}

### 13. Buy SMEA.MI (10 shares @ 100.00 EUR)
# @name buySmea
POST {{baseUrl}}/portfolios/{{portfolioId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "asset_id": "{{assetId}}",
  "type": "buy",
  "quantity": 10,
  "price": 100.00,
  "date": "2024-01-15T00:00:00Z"
}

### 14. Buy SXR8.DE (5 shares @ 300.00 EUR)
# @name buySxr8
POST {{baseUrl}}/portfolios/{{portfolioId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "asset_id": "{{asset2Id}}",
  "type": "buy",
  "quantity": 5,
  "price": 300.00,
  "date": "2024-01-15T00:00:00Z"
}

### 14bis. NEW (I.9) — List transactions, paginated: envelope
### {transactions[], total, limit, offset}. limit defaults to 20 and is clamped
### to 100, offset defaults to 0; non-numeric or negative params → 400. Stable
### ordering date DESC, created_at DESC, id DESC. Ownership enforced: 403 on
### someone else's portfolio, 404 on a missing one.
# @name listTransactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/portfolios/{{portfolioId}}/transactions?limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Portfolio class allocation (baseline to reconcile with geography/sector).
### Cost basis: SMEA.MI 1000 EUR + SXR8.DE 1500 EUR = 2500 EUR, all FX-ok. Without
### the price seed the weights are all 0 — run tests/seed-prices.sql first to see
### non-zero values.
# @name classAllocation
GET {{baseUrl}}/portfolios/{{portfolioId}}/allocation/class
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. NEW — Portfolio geographic allocation: 10 canonical regions zero-filled, in
### canonical order; "Other" only when a value could not be assigned. Weights sum
### to ~100 (FX-ok holdings are the denominator, matching /allocation/class).
### Without the price seed the weights are 0, but the 10-region structure is visible.
# @name geographyAllocation
GET {{baseUrl}}/portfolios/{{portfolioId}}/allocation/geography
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. NEW — Portfolio sector allocation: 11 canonical GICS sectors zero-filled,
### in canonical order; "Other" only when a value could not be assigned. Without
### the price seed the weights are 0, but the 11-sector structure is visible.
# @name sectorAllocation
GET {{baseUrl}}/portfolios/{{portfolioId}}/allocation/sector
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}